    "content": "<div class=\"ml-en\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">MKT101 · Chapter 10 · Session 26</span>\n<h2>Session 26 — Chapter 10: Pricing: Understanding and Capturing Customer Value</h2>\n<p class=\"nhan\">Source: FLM syllabus 13458 · session plan</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">MKT101 · Chương 10 · Buổi 26</span>\n<h2>Buổi 26 — Chapter 10: Pricing: Understanding and Capturing Customer Value</h2>\n<p class=\"nhan\">Nguồn: syllabus FLM 13458 · kế hoạch buổi</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><div class=\"kv-grid\">\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Type</span><span class=\"v\">Offline</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">LO</span><span class=\"v\">LO6</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">ITU</span><span class=\"v\">IT</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Slides in this lesson</span><span class=\"v\">none from FLM</span></div>\n</div></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><div class=\"kv-grid\">\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Hình thức</span><span class=\"v\">Offline</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">LO</span><span class=\"v\">LO6</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">ITU</span><span class=\"v\">IT</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Slide trong bài</span><span class=\"v\">FLM không có</span></div>\n</div></div>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>What this session covers (FLM, verbatim)</h3></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>Nội dung buổi học (FLM, nguyên văn)</h3></div>\n<p>Chapter 10: Pricing: Understanding and Capturing Customer Value<br><br>(Only instruct the students on What is a Price &amp; Major Pricing Strategies. Other contents can be used as topics of further discussion)</p>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>Materials to read</h3></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>Tài liệu cần đọc</h3></div>\n<p>Student's book, CMS</p>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>Constructive questions — answer them yourself first</h3></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>Câu hỏi kiến tạo — tự trả lời trước</h3></div>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>10.1</strong> — How important is pricing to the firm's performance?</li>\n<li><strong>10.2</strong> — An Armani black T-shirt costs $275, whereas a similar one from Gap or H&amp;M costs $14.9 and $7.9 respectivly. Customers who purchase Armani T-shirt are paying for a T-shrit made of 70 percent nylon, 25 percent polyester, and 5 percent elastane, whereas the Gap and H&amp;M shrits are made mainly of cotton. True, the Armani T is a bit more stylishly cut than the other two and sports a “Made in Italy” label, but how does it command a $275.00 price tag? How can Armani set such high price that customers are willing to pay? What are the differences among the pricing approaches used by Armani, and H&amp;M and Gap?</li>\n<li><strong>10.3</strong> — Why is it difficult for firms to employ value-based pricing?</li>\n<li><strong>10.4</strong> — Why is copst-plus pricing still being employed by several companies despite of its limitations?</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><div class=\"note-ct\">📝 Detailed lecture and 🎬 video for this session: coming later. For now follow the slides, the materials and the tasks above.</div></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><div class=\"note-ct\">📝 Bài giảng chi tiết và 🎬 video cho buổi này: sẽ bổ sung sau. Trước mắt học theo slide, tài liệu và nhiệm vụ ở trên.</div></div>"
